This educational resource provides a comprehensive overview of the systems analysis and design field, focusing on the Systems Development Life Cycle (SDLC) as a core framework. The text illustrates the multiple roles of a systems analyst and the skills necessary to succeed in transforming business needs into effective technical solutions. The book also reviews how to initiate projects by formulating system requests and conducting feasibility studies to evaluate economic and technical returns. The content focuses on practical aspects by presenting realistic case studies, such as the "Tune Source" company, to train students on applying concepts. This curriculum aims to ensure the construction of software systems that provide real value to organizations and efficiently meet user expectations.

