Welcome. As your engineering consultant and technical mentor, I am very happy to lead this knowledge journey. I have analyzed the 16 attached resources (which cover Object-Oriented Analysis and Design OOAD, Clean Architecture, Design Patterns, Domain-Driven Design DDD, Systems Engineering, and Security), in addition to resources related to your environment (such as Prompt Engineering and database performance).
I have designed the "Architectural Excellence Curriculum" for you. This curriculum aims to transition you from a "code writer" to a "systems engineer" possessing a holistic vision.
Here is the proposed index of ideas and concepts, arranged to build knowledge cumulatively:
Unit One: Foundations of Abstraction
Lesson 1: Essence of OO & Interface Separation.
Synthesis of concepts: Encapsulation, Information Hiding, and Program to an Interface, not an Implementation.
Resources: Object-Oriented Thought Process, Design Patterns (GoF), OOAD.
Lesson 2: SOLID Principles and Cohesion.
Synthesis of concepts: Single Responsibility Principle (SRP), Open/Closed Principle (OCP), and Component Cohesion criteria.
Resources: Clean Architecture, Software Engineering.
Unit Two: Construction Strategies & Patterns
Lesson 3: Composition over Inheritance and Creational Patterns.
Synthesis of concepts: Risks of deep inheritance, favoring composition, and Factory and Builder patterns.
Resources: Design Patterns (GoF), The Object-Oriented Thought Process.
Lesson 4: Structural & Behavioral Patterns.
Synthesis of concepts: Adapter, Facade, and Strategy for separating algorithms from context.
Resources: Design Patterns (GoF), OOAD.
Unit Three: Clean Architecture & Boundaries
Lesson 5: The Dependency Rule & Architectural Boundaries.
Synthesis of concepts: Layers, Hexagonal Architecture, and protecting the "Core" from "Details".
Resources: Clean Architecture, Software Engineering.
Lesson 6: Humble Objects & Presenters.
Synthesis of concepts: Separating testable logic from the UI and external systems.
Resources: Clean Architecture.
Unit Four: Domain-Driven Design
Lesson 7: Ubiquitous Language & Bounded Contexts.
Synthesis of concepts: Modeling business language within code, and separating models based on semantic context.
Resources: Domain-Driven Design (Evans).
Lesson 8: Entities, Value Objects, & Repositories.
Synthesis of concepts: Identity versus descriptive value, and object lifecycle.
Resources: Domain-Driven Design (Evans), OOAD.
Unit Five: Security & Quality
Lesson 9: Security by Design & Input Validation.
Synthesis of concepts: Boundary Validation, Session Management, and the principle of least privilege.
Resources: Web Application Hacker’s Handbook, OWASP Testing Guide.
Lesson 10: Requirements Engineering & SDLC.
Synthesis of concepts: Analysis versus Design, change management, and development strategies (Agile vs Waterfall).
Resources: Systems Analysis and Design, Software Engineering.

