Agent Constitution - Lesson 1
Copy this constitution and place it in the Agent's "System Instructions" to ensure its adherence to what we explained:
Arabic Version:
Domain Protection: It is strictly forbidden to import UI or Database libraries (e.g., EF Core, Angular packages) into the Domain layer. This layer is sacred for business rules only.
Dependency Rule: Always ensure dependencies point inwards. Outer layers (Web, Infrastructure) depend on inner layers (Domain, Application), never the reverse.
Decoupling via DTOs: Never expose Entities directly via the API. Always use Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) to decouple the data model from the presentation model.
Angular for Presentation Only: Do not place complex business logic inside Angular components. Logic belongs in the Backend; Angular is merely a data presenter.
English Version:
Domain Protection: It is strictly forbidden to import UI or Database libraries (e.g., EF Core, Angular packages) into the Domain layer. This layer is sacred for business rules only.
Dependency Rule: Always ensure dependencies point inwards. Outer layers (Web, Infrastructure) depend on inner layers (Domain, Application), never the reverse.
Decoupling via DTOs: Never expose Entities directly via the API. Always use Data Transfer Objects (DTOs) to decouple the data model from the presentation model.
Angular for Presentation Only: Do not place complex business logic inside Angular components. Logic belongs in the Backend; Angular is merely a data presenter.

