Here is the proposed Curriculum Index for the "Integrated Architectural Excellence" curriculum, designed to take you from abstract basics to deep strategic application:
Unit One: Architectural Foundation and Separation of Concerns
Lesson 1: The Essence of Clean Architecture & Dependency Rule.
Concept: Centrality of business rules and protecting them from external details (UI/DB)
.
Projection onto your environment: How ABP strictly applies layered architecture (Domain, Application, Infrastructure), and why Angular components must be completely isolated from Database logic.
Lesson 2: Object Thinking & Boundaries.
Concept: The difference between Data Structures and true Objects with behavior
, and the concept of Encapsulation
.
Projection onto your environment: The danger of an "Anemic Domain Model" in ASP.NET, and how to protect Entities in ABP from turning into mere data tables.
Unit Two: Strategic Design & Domain Depth
Lesson 3: Ubiquitous Language & Bounded Contexts.
Concept: Using a shared language between developers and domain experts, and dividing the system into isolated contexts to reduce complexity
,
.
Projection onto your environment: How to reflect "business language" in the names of Services and Components in Angular, and how to manage Modules in ABP as independent Bounded Contexts.
Lesson 4: Tactical Patterns: Aggregates & Repositories.
Concept: Ensuring data consistency through Aggregates as transaction boundaries, and separating data access methods
,
.
Projection onto your environment: When to use IRepository in ABP and when to avoid it? And how to design an Aggregate Root that prevents data conflicts in a SQL Server environment.
Unit Three: Construction Quality & Performance
Lesson 5: Query Performance & Indexing Strategies.
Concept: The impact of query and index design on database performance, and understanding Execution Plans
,
.
Projection onto your environment: How using LINQ and Entity Framework in ABP affects the generated SQL, and how to improve the performance of list queries in Angular interfaces.
Lesson 6: Defensive Security & Validation.
Concept: Boundary Validation and Defense in Depth principle to prevent vulnerabilities
.
Projection onto your environment: The difference between Validation in Angular (for experience improvement) and Validation in DTOs and Domain (for real security) within ABP.

